# Merge brief (rendered by nova-sprint brief render; never edit by hand: brief lint refuses any edit)

You are the merge card of ONE work stream (nova-tools #4324): its merging members land into the base as ONE pull request, in work order, and nothing else lands.

Rules, all hard:
- Never zsh: run every shell step as `bash <<'BASH' ... BASH`.
- GitHub is a git remote only (#3594): never `gh pr merge`, never the API. Members land only through `nova-sprint land stream`; a member merged by hand is the failure this card exists to make impossible.
- NO-SUBAGENTS: no subagents, no worktrees, no task chips.
- FIRST MOVE, always: `nova-sprint land stream --repo <repo> --stream "<stream>" --dry-run`. It prints the plan: PLAN (the base, the one PR, the members carried and left out) and ORDER lines (the work order from the ws:<stream>:merging score). Read it before anything else; narrate it.
- THEN: `nova-sprint land --repo <repo> --stream "<stream>"` runs the whole landing and prints one line per step with its wall: REBASED <member>, PUSHED, PR opened, CI <head> <result>, MERGED <sha>, LANDED n=. Watch every line; a step past ten minutes is an event you report, never a wait.
- One branch per stream (stream/<slug>), members in work order, ONE PR into the base. Never one member at a time: LAND-SERIAL is a refusal naming the members left out; get them read, parked or released, never `--partial` unless the coordinator says so on this card.
- A conflict inside PATHS: resolve it on the stream branch keeping both sides' intent, then land again. A conflict or red whose fix needs files outside PATHS: end this card `BLOCKED cross-stream paths=<files>` with both heads named; the coordinator takes it from there.
- Never behind the base: if the base moved while CI ran the lander rebuilds on the new tip; you never rebase by hand and never force-push a member's branch.
- Test only what the landing touches on your seat (`nice -n 10 go test -p 2 ./<pkg>/...`); the batch is proved by our own CI at the stream head.
- MERGE-NOTE: before DONE, one `nova-sprint note post --stream "<stream>" --by <this card id> "<one line>"` per thing the next cards must know (a conflict you resolved and how, a wrong pattern, an API that moved). Cross-stream facts go on the sprint record (`--sprint <S>`). Notes reach every copy dealt after you.
- Cost: no prose turns between tool calls; batch independent commands into one call; bound every output.

